# Wire OpCode (data plane, `delivery/errors`)

Import with alias: `deliveryerrors ".../internal/delivery/errors"` (package name `errors`).

## `internal/delivery/errors` files

| File | Range | API |
|------|----------|-----|
| `join_reject.go` | `0x40–0x5F` (+ reservation via join) | `JoinRejectOpCode`, `SendJoinReject` |
| `reservation_reject.go` | `0x70–0x7F` | `mapReservationRejectOpCode` (join-reject path only; no standalone sender) |
| `join_reject.go` (in-room) | `0x60–0x6F` | `InRoomErrorOpCode` wrapper (frames go via `Room.Send`/`peer.Deliver`) |
| `domain/opcodes.go` + `NewPeerNotificationFrame` | `0x80+` | Room notifications — sent by **usecase** via `room.Send` (not delivery/errors): `OpPeerDisconnected`/`OpPeerReconnected`, payload `peerID u64 BE` (P20); `OpRoomClosed` `0x82` (P29) — room closed by the server (no-migration deploy, P33: host left), empty payload, disconnect follows the frame; sent via `peer.Deliver` from usecase teardown |

Domain: `opcodes.go`, `join_errors.go`, `reservation_error.go`, `room_errors.go` (`InRoomErrorOpCode`).

`ErrPeerStale` — internal-only sentinel (identity-scoped registry lifecycle, P20): no wire opcode and none is added — unreachable before the reject frame (would map to `OpInternal`).

